{
  "version": 1,
  "project": "madelon-reanalysis",
  "reason": "The first fleet: three agents on boost, stable-forest and vote at once (live/madelon-fleet-*), each with the project_map tool, from 15:14 to the launcher's wall clock of 1,800 seconds. Every trail checks. Nothing is resolved. No run wrote out/metrics.json: each agent explored with printed diagnostics (10, 16 and 22 steps), so no observation has measures and none can meet screen, the milestone all three wait on. The agents did not use each other. Each read the map once, at its first step, before any sibling had an observation, and never again. boost's two plans build on live-2 step-7, the established miss, not on a sibling. Two weaknesses of the fleet itself, found in the run: vote listed the directory that holds every agent's workspace (step-5), which an agent could read to get round the withholding; no command read a sibling's file, by a search of every command in the three session files. And each agent opened data/heldout.csv while looking around (row counts and headers), against its brief's rule, so a holding resolution citing any of these trails would fail check. The map stands as rev-7 left it.",
  "triggered_by": [
    "probe:madelon-fleet-boost@sha256:7c4a257bae6a262b97ace3ab6ed78a0e4d81be83099e2749cc28116c86047150#step-9",
    "probe:madelon-fleet-stable-forest@sha256:92cd6d200c1ad3f29df883554540eca17392a5261f2b02c250606fcbf91dece4#step-15",
